    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "4 Determination of the electrical parameters  "
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 64,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 54.667, 391.361, 287.667, 450.223 ],
    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Looking at (1) gives us the needed electrical parameters to be defined. We find R   and L , the resistance and the inductance of the coil, µ f , the force constant, and µ bemf , the bemf (back electromagnetic force) constant of the system."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 67,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 55.0, 340.223, 287.667, 389.89 ],
    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "R   and L   are the intrinsic electrical properties of the   coil and are purely passive. A simple measurement on the RLC meter will allow us to get those values. These are given in Table 3. The quantities µ   and µ   are representative of the"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 69,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 55.333, 305.89, 288.333, 341.557 ],
    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "f bemf same phenomenon – the expression of the Lorentz force – but have neither the same causes nor the same effects."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 70,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 55.0, 255.223, 284.667, 305.223 ],
    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Lorentz expresses that the charge carriers of a conductor immersed in a (non-collinear) magnetic field are subjected to a force when moving and this according to the following relation:"
  }, {
